  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the presence of a sure outcome in one of the lotteries to apply, but neither lottery has such an outcome. Furthermore, the individual did not consider certainty or sure payoffs in their deliberation; instead, they focused on the relative probabilities of winning and accepted a lower prize for a higher chance. There is no indication that the individual was guided by the presence (or absence) of a guaranteed outcome, which is the core of the decision reason. Therefore, both the relevant information (sure outcomes) and the decision rule (prefer the lottery with a sure outcome) are absent from the individual’s reasoning.",
